|info = 
*Wisp expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''25''' [[energy]] to tear open and sustains a portal to the sun to harness its destructive power. While sustaining the portal, Wisp focuses the solar plasma into a single beam with curving flares over a length of {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''40''' meters; the beam possesses infinite [[Punch Through]] against enemy bodies, and inflicts {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''500 / 550 / 625 / 750''' damage '''alternating''' between {{D|Heat}} and {{D|Radiation}} every '''half''' second with a <u>'''100%'''</u> [[status chance]] of the respective element type. Each enemy that receives damage from the beam becomes individually more vulnerable to the respective element dealt by the beam, with beam damage increasing by <u>'''100%'''</u> per hit of an element up to a maximum of <u>'''1000%'''</u>, meaning it takes up to '''10 seconds''' of sustained damage to '''each''' enemy to maximize the damage they receive. Press the ability key (default {{Keybind|4}}) while active to deactivate this ability.
**Damage Ramp is a per-damge-type, per-enemy debuff that persists until the ability is deactivated.
**Wisp recoils backward when the ability deactivates.
**Holding the fire button (default {{Keybind|LMB}}) doubles the beam's base damage to {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''1,000 / 1,100 / 1,250 / 1,500''' per hit. Wisp's movement speed is slowed by <u>'''50%'''</u> while boosting Sol Gate.
***It can be more energy efficient to debuff targets before activating this level of the ability, as the damage ramp is unaffected by it.
**Damage is unaffected by {{Arcane|Arcane Arachne|mod damage bonuses}}, but '''is''' affected by body part multipliers such as headshots.
**Sol Gate consumes {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}{{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''12''' energy per second ({{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}{{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''24''' energy per second during the boosted version) while active and will remain active until Wisp's energy is depleted or the ability is deactivated by pressing the ability key again.
***Activation energy cost is affected by [[Ability Efficiency]], and the energy drain is affected by [[Ability Efficiency]] and [[Ability Duration]].
***Wisp '''cannot''' replenish energy using {{A|Energy Vampire}}, [[Rift Plane]]'s innate energy regeneration, [[Squad Energy Restore]]s, {{M|Energy Siphon}}, {{M|Energy Nexus}}, {{M|Dreamer's Bond}}, and/or {{Focus|Wellspring}} while Sol Gate is active.
***Energy can be replenished by [[Pickups#Orbs|Energy Orbs]], {{Arcane|Arcane Energize}}, [[Orokin Void]] [[Death Orb]] energy restores, {{M|Rage}}, and/or {{M|Hunter Adrenaline}} while the ability is active.
***Sol Gate's energy drain is '''not''' converted into shields by [[Set Mods#Augur Mod Set|Augur Mods]].
*Wisp cannot cast Reservoirs or Breach Surge, perform parkour [[Maneuvers]] or sprinting except dodge rolls, or other general interactions while channeling this ability.
*Wisp is immune to [[knockdown]] while channeling this ability.
*Energy beams, energy particles, and energy surge color tinting are affected by Wisp's chosen Warframe energy color.
| synergies =
*Currently obtained Motes from {{A|Reservoirs}} provide additional properties to Sol Gate.
**'''Vitality:''' Provides a <u>'''25%'''</u> damage increase.
**'''Haste:''' Allows Sol Gate to deal {{D|Corrosive}} procs on every damage instance.
***Does '''not''' gain {{D|Corrosive}} damage.
**'''Shock:''' Provides a <u>'''25%'''</u> damage increase.
***Mote Damage bonuses add together to <u>'''50%'''</u>, a multiplicative bonus to Sol Gate's final damage.
**Reservoir Motes orbiting Wisp will instead orbit around the portal. When Sol Gate is deactivated, Motes will return to Wisp again.
*{{A|Wil-O-Wisp}} can be cast during Sol Gate to cloak, spawn a clone and teleport to it when desired.
*Has an increased (<u>'''?%'''</u>) chance to trigger {{A|Breach Surge}}'s surge spark.
